# Build-context hygiene for a frontend-rooted context only. Both shipped images
# build from the repository root, so the root .dockerignore is what Docker
# consults for them; this list applies when a build is invoked against this
# directory instead.
#
# Because it is not load-bearing for the shipped images, an over-exclusion here
# fails silently and late. Only generated, transient and machine-local material
# is listed: nothing that `npm ci`, `ng build` or `ng test` reads may be added,
# and version-control patterns are enumerated rather than globbed so no `.git*`
# wildcard can reach an asset under public/. There are no negation entries, so
# no later line can shadow an earlier one.

# Installed dependencies - the single most important entry. The frontend image
# runs `npm ci` inside its build stage, so a host tree copied in would ship
# wrong-platform native bindings and defeat the deterministic lockfile install.
**/node_modules/

# Build output and compiler caches. The production bundle is produced inside the
# image, never copied in; out-tsc/ is the TypeScript outDir.
**/dist/
**/.angular/
out-tsc/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test and coverage output.
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/
karma-results*
chrome-profiler-events*.json
speed-measure-plugin*.json

# Logs and package-manager caches.
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.eslintcache
.npm/

# Version-control metadata, enumerated exactly and anchored at the context root.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Editor and operating-system noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/ehthumbs.db
**/Desktop.ini

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local environment overrides and credentials.
#
# Matched by FAMILY, never by enumerated suffix: `**/.env*` closes the whole
# family at every depth, including `.env.production` and `.env.development`,
# and mirrors the repository-root .dockerignore that governs the context
# docker/frontend.Dockerfile actually builds from.
#
# The workspace's real committed configuration lives in src/environments/
# (environment.ts and environment.development.ts) and is deliberately NOT
# matched: `**/.env*` requires a basename beginning with a literal dot, which
# those files do not have, so the production build keeps every file it needs.
# Every other pattern in this group is keyed to a credential extension that no
# workspace source file uses.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env*
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.p8
*.jks
*.keystore
*.ppk
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.p8
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.ppk

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .editorconfig, README.md and this file itself stay in the context. Every
# additional entry here is one more chance to silently drop something a
# frontend-rooted build needs.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
